        "username": "awp832",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-09-23T01:07:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>&nbsp;So some people had discussed doing a Villain gauntlet sort of thing,&nbsp; just for fun, where you keep all your stuff and current HP and just play one villain after the next after the next.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Well I dont know if there's an official way to do this, but what I did was after picking team:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>1.&nbsp; Choose Villain and environment, must be different from what you've played before, if possible..&nbsp;&nbsp; (if you pick Insula Primalis for your first game, you cant choose Insula Primalis again until you've done all the environments).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp; All Ongoing and Equipment cards remain in play, even \"temporary\" ongoings (Bloody Knucles, End of Days, Heroic Interception and the like).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>3.&nbsp; No healing in between rounds.</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp; All cards in hand and trash reshuffled into Hero deck.&nbsp;&nbsp; Heroes draw new hands of 4 cards each.</p><p>5.&nbsp; all on advanced mode, btw.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I sorta expected this to be hard, but actually it was pretty easy.&nbsp;&nbsp; My team had a lot of healing and utility,&nbsp;&nbsp; AA, Fixer, Tempest, Young Legacy (in that order).&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Started out with Ambuscade on Rook City.&nbsp; Wanted an easier villain that doesnt kill stuff so I could build things up, and decided I may as well knock the hardest environment out of the picture.&nbsp;&nbsp; Near Flawless Victory here, with only Legacy down a few HP, and a good amount of stuff on the table.&nbsp; By the time I got through killing Baron Blade on Mars I had a copy of just about everything down in every heroes deck, except for a few of AAs cards and Gene-bound shackles, which I never really in the first few games.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>From there I beat up Plague Rat in the Toumb of Anubis, Spite (before he even touched a drug!) on Insula Primalis, AkashBhuta on Megalopolis, The Chairman/Operative on Atlantis,&nbsp; Voss on the Industrial complex, and the Ennead on the Realm of Discord.&nbsp;&nbsp; I haven't actually lost yet, and currently AA is my lowest HP hero at 20.&nbsp; But I'm out of time, so I set things aside for now.&nbsp;&nbsp; I think the only real challenging villain left is Matriarch, and I don't anticipate that many problems. &nbsp; I'm pretty sure I can beat everyone. &nbsp; With ultimate setups you can just cleave through villain hp.&nbsp;&nbsp; Kinda fun,&nbsp; dunno if it's something I'd want to do too often tho.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I'll see if I get the all-kill.&nbsp; Anyone else tried the Villain Gauntlet?</p>",
