        "raw": "<p>&nbsp;So some people had discussed doing a Villain gauntlet sort of thing,&nbsp; just for fun, where you keep all your stuff and current HP and just play one villain after the next after the next.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Well I dont know if there&#39;s an official way to do this, but what I did was after picking team:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>1.&nbsp; Choose Villain and environment, must be different from what you&#39;ve played before, if possible..&nbsp;&nbsp; (if you pick Insula Primalis for your first game, you cant choose Insula Primalis again until you&#39;ve done all the environments).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp; All Ongoing and Equipment cards remain in play, even &quot;temporary&quot; ongoings (Bloody Knucles, End of Days, Heroic Interception and the like).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>3.&nbsp; No healing in between rounds.</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp; All cards in hand and trash reshuffled into Hero deck.&nbsp;&nbsp; Heroes draw new hands of 4 cards each.</p><p>5.&nbsp; all on advanced mode, btw.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I sorta expected this to be hard, but actually it was pretty easy.&nbsp;&nbsp; My team had a lot of healing and utility,&nbsp;&nbsp; AA, Fixer, Tempest, Young Legacy (in that order).&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Started out with Ambuscade on Rook City.&nbsp; Wanted an easier villain that doesnt kill stuff so I could build things up, and decided I may as well knock the hardest environment out of the picture.&nbsp;&nbsp; Near Flawless Victory here, with only Legacy down a few HP, and a good amount of stuff on the table.&nbsp; By the time I got through killing Baron Blade on Mars I had a copy of just about everything down in every heroes deck, except for a few of AAs cards and Gene-bound shackles, which I never really in the first few games.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>From there I beat up Plague Rat in the Toumb of Anubis, Spite (before he even touched a drug!) on Insula Primalis, AkashBhuta on Megalopolis, The Chairman/Operative on Atlantis,&nbsp; Voss on the Industrial complex, and the Ennead on the Realm of Discord.&nbsp;&nbsp; I haven&#39;t actually lost yet, and currently AA is my lowest HP hero at 20.&nbsp; But I&#39;m out of time, so I set things aside for now.&nbsp;&nbsp; I think the only real challenging villain left is Matriarch, and I don&#39;t anticipate that many problems. &nbsp; I&#39;m pretty sure I can beat everyone. &nbsp; With ultimate setups you can just cleave through villain hp.&nbsp;&nbsp; Kinda fun,&nbsp; dunno if it&#39;s something I&#39;d want to do too often tho.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I&#39;ll see if I get the all-kill.&nbsp; Anyone else tried the Villain Gauntlet?</p>",
