        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/8baadc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-09-23T05:25:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We did a very similar type of game.  We had one person put a piece of paper with a number underneath each environment deck randomly. Then the villains were each assigned a number by a different person at random. The heroes “picked” which environment to fight in, and whatever villain had the same number was the one we fought. It was a lot of fun and always a surprise. But we continued till we were out of villains. We also found that keeping all equipment was way too easy, but compromised on keeping one piece of equipment/ongoing out or regaining 5hp.  It worked out well. Although we were able to kill citizen dawn in one shot thanks to bunker charging up for three villains.</p>",
